{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Your sons have fainted.</b> Like ויתעלף (Jonah 4:8)." "<b>They lie.</b> By famine and sword." "<b>Like a turtledove [כתוא].</b> Like עוף, and there is nothing wrong with it. (And the meaning is כתוא מכמר.) And behold, it is in construct state with מכמר, like יפלו במכמוריו (Psalms 141:10)." "<b>The rebuke [גערת].</b> It is His wrath."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {2 "The parenthetical והטעם גערת is marked as a small gloss in the source; it indicates the word's meaning rather than a separate comment.", 3 "The small parenthetical והטעם כתוא מכמר belongs structurally within comment [2] per the source marking; the parenthetical here appears misplaced in the provided text but is rendered as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:06.985618371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}